# Hodd guard — track only this file, the README, and *.example shapes.
# Everything else beneath Hodd is private and must never be committed.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!*.example
!*.example.md

# 2026-11-02 (RULES/42) — the sentence above says "*.example shapes", and until today that
# was true only at the top of hodd/: `*` swallowed the directory itself, so a template could
# not sit beside the shelf whose file it teaches, and `hodd/data/operator.md.example` was
# refused by this very guard. The intent was right; the pattern did not implement it. `!*/`
# lets git look INTO a sub-shelf, where `*` still ignores every file and the two negations
# above still admit only the shapes.
!*/
